TI  - Radiologic manifestations of bronchoscopic lung volume reduction in severe 
      chronic obstructive pulmonary disease.
PG  - 475-86
LID - 10.2214/AJR.14.13185 [doi]
AB  - OBJECTIVE. Bronchoscopic lung volume reduction promises to become an effective 
      treatment option in severe chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. Several 
      techniques are currently being investigated, including implantation of devices 
      into the lung and instillation of hot water vapor or polymer. This article 
      reviews the spectrum of radiologic manifestations on chest radiography and CT 
      that occur after the intervention. CONCLUSION. Familiarity with the intended 
      effects and adverse events will aid the radiologist in supporting bronchoscopic 
      lung volume reduction.
