TI  - Future Treatment of Emphysema with Roles for Valves, Novel Strategies and Lung 
      Volume Reduction Surgery.
PG  - 221-227
LID - S1547-4127(21)00007-4 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.thorsurg.2021.02.003 [doi]
AB  - Although there are multiple pharmacologic and nonpharmacological options to 
      alleviate symptoms of emphysema, none of these treatment modalities halts disease 
      progression. The expanding disease burden has led to development of innovative 
      therapeutic strategies that also aim to induce lung volume reduction. 
      Bronchoscopic lung volume reduction originated in 2001 and has continued to grow 
      rapidly ever since. This article discusses more recent developments in 
      bronchoscopic and novel interventions and speculates on how these novel 
      strategies may impact the future of lung reduction interventions.
