DP  - 2025 Jul
TI  - [Therapeutic Experience with Three-port Thoracoscopic Lung Volume Reduction 
      Surgery for Emphysema].
PG  - 541-545
AB  - Lung volume reduction surgery( LVRS) and lung transplantation have proven to be 
      effective surgical treatments for emphysema. However, since the results of the 
      National Emphysema Treatment Trial (NETT) study, there has been a sharp decline 
      in the number of LVRS cases in Japan, and few patients are eligible for lung 
      transplantation due to donor problems, so bronchoscopic lung volume reduction 
      (BLVR) is expected to be an effective treatment in the future. In our department, 
      LVRS was performed in 22 cases out of approximately 10,000 thoracoscopic 
      procedures from 1999 to 2024. The overall postoperative forced expiratory volume 
      in on second (FEV1.0) improvement rate was 45%, especially 61% for bilateral 
      surgery. If postoperative complications can be safely controlled, LVRS can be 
      expected to have better outcomes than BLVR for bilateral upper lobe dominant 
      forms of emphysema.
