TI  - Fibroblast growth factor-2 promotes recovery of pulmonary function in a canine 
      models of elastase-induced emphysema.
PG  - 15-26
AB  - Bronchoscopic lung volume reduction (BLVR) for severe emphysema is less invasive 
      than lung volume reduction surgery. Fibroblast growth factor-2 (FGF-2) has been 
      reported to enhance fibrogenesis and angiogenesis. The aim of this study was to 
      investigate the feasibility of BLVR with the FGF-2, and ability to reduce lung 
      volume and promote recovery of lung function. The BLVR based on FGF-2 is less 
      invasive than surgical procedures, and can be performed repeatedly if the 
      effectiveness of volume reduction is inadequate. This simple bronchoscopic 
      approach allows selective reduction in the volume of the emphysematous 
      parenchyma, and intratracheal administration of FGF-2 induces an increase in 
      pulmonary blood flow, thus allowing recovery of pulmonary function.
